      "question": "What is the TMAZ?",
      "status": "complete",
      "browser_total_ms": 1222.0,
      "browser_first_visible_ms": 796.5,
      "backend_total_ms": 582,
      "timing_caption": "Search 28 ms \u00b7 Rerank 85 ms \u00b7 Generate 466 ms \u00b7 First text 485 ms \u00b7 Total 582 ms",
      "answer_words": 55,
      "answer": "The Thermo\u2011Mechanically Affected Zone (TMAZ) is the region adjacent to the Stir Zone (SZ) that experiences mechanical deformation and plastic flow during friction stir welding. It is plastically deformed but does not recrystallize, unlike the SZ. The TMAZ\u2019s microstructure is inhomogeneous, with reduced high\u2011angle grain boundaries and a hardness minimum relative to the SZ. [1][2]",
